.TH SKOGAI-CONFIG 1  "skogai-config 0.0.0" 
.SH NAME
skogai\-config \- read and write key/value config across system, global, local and module layers
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBskogai config\fR <COMMAND>
.SH DESCRIPTION
.br
read and write key/value config across system, global, local and module layers
.br

.br
fold order, later wins: module.md `config:` defaults, system, global, local,
.br
module.local.md overrides, \-\-file layers, then SKOGAI_* env.
.br
a module's keys are mounted under its name: runner's `model` is `runner.model`.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
skogai\-config\-get(1)
print the resolved value of a key; a list prints one item per line
.TP
skogai\-config\-set(1)
set a key in the local layer, the global one, a module's module.local.md or a \-\-file's .local.md
.TP
skogai\-config\-unset(1)
remove a key from the local layer, the global one, a module's module.local.md or a \-\-file's .local.md
.TP
skogai\-config\-list(1)
print every resolved key as key=value; a list prints one line per item
.TP
skogai\-config\-env(1)
print the resolved config as export lines; a list's items are newline\-separated
.TP
skogai\-config\-files(1)
print the path of each layer file, and whether it exists
.SH "ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES:"
.TP
\fISKOGAI_SYSTEM_DIR\fR [default: /etc/skogai]
.br
dir of the system layer config
.TP
\fISKOGAI_CONFIG_DIR\fR
.br
dir of the global layer, default ~/.config/skogai
.TP
\fISKOGAI_LOCAL_DIR\fR [default: .skogai]
.br
dir of the local layer; relative is from the git root, or pwd
.TP
\fISKOGAI_MODULE_PATH\fR
.br
colon\-separated dirs of module sources, default the one this module sits in
